- **Click limits.** A short link can be created with an optional `max_clicks` (@@MIN_VALUE_COMMAS@@ to @@MAX_VALUE_COMMAS@@): after that many redirects the short URL answers 410. The link details show `max_clicks` and `remaining_clicks`, and a used-up link reports the new status `exhausted`. Links without a limit, existing links and existing API clients are unaffected (additive API change; their JSON is unchanged). The limit is enforced by one atomic conditional UPDATE, so `max_clicks` of 1 never redirects twice. The new migration `@@MIGRATION_PATH@@` adds a nullable `links.max_clicks`; undo it with a forward fix (see `docs/features/max-clicks.md`). Regenerate `docs/api.md` with `python -m shortener.apidoc` if it was not part of the change.
